.TH ESP32-MONITOR 1 "August 2026" "esp32-monitor 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esp32-monitor \- btop-style live ESP32 serial monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esp32-monitor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esp32-monitor
reads newline-delimited JSON telemetry from an ESP32 over a serial port
and renders a full-screen terminal dashboard. It shows CPU clock and
per-core usage, uptime, heap, Wi-Fi RSSI, serial/network rates, optional
chip/PSRAM/temperature fields, and a live FreeRTOS task list.
.PP
Tasks can be selected with the keyboard. Kill requests require
confirmation. Protected system tasks are blocked in the UI and rejected
by firmware.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPATH\fR
Serial device. Default is the configured port, or auto-detect.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-baud " " \fIRATE\fR
Baud rate. Default 115200.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-theme " " \fINAME\fR
Color theme: default, nord, dracula, or gruvbox.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Load settings from an INI file.
.TP
.B \-\-list-ports
Print available serial ports and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Up/Down
Move the task selection.
.TP
.B PgUp/PgDn
Scroll the task list.
.TP
.B A
Toggle user tasks vs all tasks.
.TP
.B K
Request kill of the selected task.
.TP
.B Y / N
Confirm or cancel a pending kill.
.TP
.B S
Pause or resume live graphs.
.TP
.B T
Cycle built-in themes.
.TP
.B H / ?
Show the in-app help overlay.
.TP
.B Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./esp32-monitor.ini
Project-local configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/esp32-monitor/config.ini
User configuration.
.TP
.I config.example.ini
Example configuration shipped with the source tree.
.SH SEE ALSO
The ESP32 sketch in
.I esp/esp.ino
emits telemetry and enforces the protected-task deny-list.
